body:
Slice 4 of 6 of #635. Depends on #650 (restore calls `gc::referenced_fragments` and gates on `protects`, so this builds on the GC slice).

## What

- the remaining consumers routed through the resolver with the same per-object containment: restore, reconstruction (`assess` / `find_chunk`), backfill (resolve, or skip with a stated reason and an assertion — it rewrites the map, so a segmented record must be handled deliberately), rebalance evacuation, and `desired_state`;
- the ~55-line `check_value_ceiling` / `check_record_ceilings` helpers that `repoint_chunk` needs (carved out of #647's committer region — a repair must not silently grow a record past the 100 KB ceiling);
- the central `reconcile_step` leg of `segmented_map_consumers.rs` (it needs GC+scrub and these passes, so it ships here) and the DST repoint-versus-supersede prop;
- fixes the perf finding still open at #647's close: `find_chunk` re-reads the object root once per queued chunk (reconstruction.rs:646/:676 in the closed PR), turning the deployed custodian's repair loop from Q namespace scans into Q x N point reads — resolve once per pass, or memoize per object.

## Out of scope

The chunk-id floor (slice 5).

## Acceptance

- `RestoreReport::stranded_marked == 0` across a full reconcile step over segmented objects; a repoint respects the record ceilings;
- backfill either resolves a segmented record or skips it with reason + assertion, never rewrites it blind;
- reconstruction resolves each object's root once per pass, not once per queued chunk (asserted);
- `cargo xtask ci` green.

Part of #635 / #508 / epic #513.
